## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to implement non-recursive mergesort on a linked list, a common real-world pattern where recursion is costly or prohibited. Tests pointer manipulation, stability of merge, and correctness of bottom-up passes, plus O(n log n) time and O(1) extra space.

## Key Concepts

- Bottom-up mergesort
- In-place linked-list merge
- Stability
